# .trivyignore
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Accepted Trivy findings for clusterfactory.
#
# Every entry here is either:
#   A) a finding in a vendored upstream subchart that cannot be fixed without
#      forking (gitea-11.0.1.tgz, jenkins-5.9.9.tgz), or
#   B) a finding in clusterfactory's own templates where the behaviour is
#      intentional and the risk is explicitly accepted.
#
# Upstream subchart findings are tracked at:
#   https://github.com/clusterfactory/clusterfactory/issues/23
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Intentional: clusterfactory templates ────────────────────────────────────

# KSV053: Jenkins subchart creates broad RBAC rules for its agent provisioning.
# Cannot be modified without forking the upstream jenkins/jenkins chart.
KSV053

# KSV125: act_runner image pulled from docker.gitea.com (trusted Gitea upstream).
# Registry is not docker.io but is the official Gitea registry.
KSV125

# KSV113: Wire job requires Secret read/write access to store the runner
# registration token. This is intentional and scoped to the release namespace.
KSV113

# ── Upstream subchart: gitea-11.0.1.tgz + jenkins-5.9.9.tgz ─────────────────
# The following findings originate in the vendored upstream Gitea and Jenkins
# subcharts. clusterfactory's own templates (runner, wire job, preflight, tests)
# have all these security contexts correctly configured. The findings below
# cannot be resolved without modifying upstream chart source.
#
# They will be removed when upstream charts ship the fixes, or when the
# subcharts are upgraded to versions that include them.

# KSV001: allowPrivilegeEscalation not explicitly set to false in Gitea/Jenkins
# subchart containers.
KSV001

# KSV003: capabilities.drop ALL not set in Gitea/Jenkins subchart containers.
KSV003

# KSV004: CPU limits not set in some Gitea/Jenkins subchart init containers.
KSV004

# KSV012: runAsNonRoot not set in Gitea/Jenkins subchart containers.
KSV012

# KSV014: readOnlyRootFilesystem not set in Gitea/Jenkins subchart containers.
KSV014

# KSV020: runAsUser > 10000 not set — Gitea/Jenkins subcharts use default UIDs.
# Trivy also incorrectly flags the runner (runAsUser: 1000) despite the check
# description requiring > 10000, not exactly 10000. Tracked upstream:
# https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy/issues/8210
KSV020

# KSV021: runAsGroup > 10000 not set — same as KSV020.
KSV021

# KSV030: seccompProfile not set in Gitea/Jenkins subchart containers.
KSV030

# KSV104: Seccomp profile not specified — same as KSV030.
KSV104

# KSV106: Capabilities not restricted in Gitea/Jenkins subchart containers.
KSV106

# KSV118: Default security context in Gitea/Jenkins subchart containers.
KSV118


